+# Proof outline
+
+The theorem asks whether the reciprocal root-interaction statistic is superadditive under finite additive convolution. The exact proof DAG is stored in `proof-units.json`; its readable reconstruction is in `full-study.md`.
+
+The argument normalizes the affirmative answer wrapper, expands `FourProp`, splits the nodup and repeated-root branches of `Φ`, applies the First Proof finite Stam inequality to the coefficient-defined convolution, discharges the ENNReal top branches, and restores all universal quantifiers. No hypotheses, exceptional branches, or trust boundaries are omitted.
